 pointer. Previously it was referenced in evdi_sched_page_flip function which runs asynchronously. This sometimes leads to incrementing ref count of 0 and assertion hit, i.e. when framebuffer is removed from other thread.  Safe way of storing framebuffer is to reference it in evdi_crtc_mode_set or in evdi_crtc_page_flip.  Also refactored a bit evdi_painter_grabpix_ioctl.  BUG=chromium:596408 TEST=Manual looping through extended and rotated EVDI monitor works fine, without any system crash.  Change-Id: Iffa7d13e6e647d09ec534081d8f5801137fd6ab9 Signed-off-by: Dawid Kurek &lt;dawid.kurek@displaylink.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/333753 Tested-by: ukasz Spintzyk &lt;lukasz.spintzyk@displaylink.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Haixia Shi &lt;hshi@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit b7eefc97efc98537874a5a3a66be41f521a27c3f) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/342381 Commit-Ready: Łukasz Spintzyk &lt;lukasz.spintzyk@displaylink.com&gt; Tested-by: Łukasz Spintzyk &lt;lukasz.spintzyk@displaylink.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="342381" owner_email="szymon.kunc@displaylink.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/81/342381/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.10" change_id="Ie7d0114004341d37561fe1a9dc73d0f2e450bc2b" commit="95c0f56d063f9d594661e3166b05c4f53ffcea9e" commit_message="drm/evdi: Threadsafe reference of framebuffer count  Fixed the way how we store recentFB pointer. Previously it was referenced in evdi_sched_page_flip function which runs asynchronously. This sometimes leads to incrementing ref count of 0 and assertion hit, i.e. when framebuffer is removed from other thread.  Safe way of storing framebuffer is to reference it in evdi_crtc_mode_set or in evdi_crtc_page_flip.  Also refactored a bit evdi_painter_grabpix_ioctl.  BUG=chromium:596408 TEST=Manual looping through extended and rotated EVDI monitor works fine, without any system crash.  Change-Id: Ie7d0114004341d37561fe1a9dc73d0f2e450bc2b Signed-off-by: Szymon Kunc &lt;szymon.kunc@displaylink.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/345830 Commit-Ready: Łukasz Spintzyk &lt;lukasz.spintzyk@displaylink.com&gt; Tested-by: Łukasz Spintzyk &lt;lukasz.spintzyk@displaylink.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="345830" owner_email="szymon.kunc@displaylink.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/30/345830/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ide4dfea9250a52dd253fd98367e0d7ee1a2cf69f" commit="37b679c06de8c57c5285c88874b0c1dffce60c1e" commit_message="FIXUP: CHROMIUM: sdio: Add MMC_CAP_SDIO_IRQ support  1. Fix hung up on sdioirq issue when doing Suspend/Resume    aging test. 2. If clock is off, it will read wrong register value.    Therefore, these values can not be used for    msdc_recheck_sdio_irq function  Signed-off-by: Yong Mao &lt;yong.mao@mediatek.com&gt; BUG=chrome-os-partner:48722 TEST=build and boot oak-rev4  Change-Id: Ide4dfea9250a52dd253fd98367e0d7ee1a2cf69f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346000 Commit-Ready: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Minghsiu Tsai &lt;Minghsiu.Tsai@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346000" owner_email="yong.mao@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/00/346000/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I21aa8c70b88c0ce0f6d3f6f9b54feef91b155932" commit="6ee3f631dc0ba0254e17110024bab6c12d058f8a" commit_message="Add tnagel to OWNERS  Thiemo has authored or reviewed many of the recent changes to this repo and is also one of the most knowledgeable with regards to VPD usage (especially outside factory/firmware team applications).  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=none  Change-Id: I21aa8c70b88c0ce0f6d3f6f9b54feef91b155932 Signed-off-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/342583 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Thiemo Nagel &lt;tnagel@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="342583" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/vpd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vpd" ref="refs/changes/83/342583/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I68816aae829f9e6249302b5f88884f9996b867ff" commit="787ccf39b32ce9943d010c369ceba515c172cfe0" commit_message="Makefile: special case for CLs that only delete files.  If a CL only deletes files, then PRESUBMIT_FILES will be empty, which makes `make test-presubmit` fail since the &quot;find&quot; command will find ALL files under platform/factory that are newer than &quot;.tests-passed&quot;. Meanwhile, last modification time of &quot;./git/&quot; directory is changed when on presubmit checks, so the presubmit check never passes. In this CL, test-presubmit compares the timestamp of last CL and timestamp of .tests-passes if PRESUBMIT_FILES is empty.  BUG=None TEST=manual test  Change-Id: I68816aae829f9e6249302b5f88884f9996b867ff Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/338007 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " f